<h2>How the real transcript will be published</h2>
<ol>
  <li>The human exports the conversation from ChatGPT. The account-wide export stays private and never goes into Git.</li>
  <li>Only this one conversation is extracted locally, keeping message order, roles and whatever timestamps exist.</li>
  <li>Personal data and secrets are replaced with <code>[REDACTED: category]</code>, and every redaction is logged.</li>
  <li>The human reviews the exact public text and approves it.</li>
  <li>It's published as <code>conversation/FOUNDING-SESSION.md</code>, with a digest and an OpenTimestamps proof.</li>
</ol>
